.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Built _site/ (Netlify publish target) — produced fresh on every deploy.
_site/

# Local downloads of the DATAtourisme regional export (~45 MB, rebuilt daily).
datatourisme-reg-*.csv

# Never public: contributed photo originals (promise to the photographer).
incoming-benedicte/

.env*
*.bak
*.tmp

# Generic photo library copied from the 74 as a baseline — large binaries.
# Remove this rule if the generiques should be version-controlled here.

# Engine byproducts — regenerated on every build.
scripts/__pycache__/
reports/*
_site/

# …except the reports the gates READ. (Note `reports/*`, not `reports/` — git
# does not descend into an ignored directory, so a negation under one never
# matches.) Ignoring all of reports/ was inherited
# wholesale and is wrong here: several gates fail closed when their evidence
# file is absent, so a gate that is green on a developer's machine goes red in
# CI, where reports/ was never checked out. These are evidence, not byproducts —
# a verification result is worth nothing if it isn't kept.
!reports/i18n-verify-*.json
!reports/render-verify-*.json
!reports/i18n-leak-baseline.json
!reports/protected-placements.md
